WEBVTT

NOTE
Transcribed from the narration in this video. Every figure the
speaker states matches the OECD time-use data behind this page.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
G'day.

2
00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.420
Want to see my day?

3
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.560
It's pretty even, actually.

4
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.220
I start with 10 hours and
58 minutes of personal care.

5
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.260
Sleep, meals, getting ready.

6
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.560
That's just 8 minutes below the 35
country average, right in the middle.

7
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.120
Then work, 3 hours and
58 minutes of paid work.

8
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.920
After that, 4 hours and 3
minutes of unpaid work at home.

9
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.400
45 minutes above average.

10
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.480
And then 4 hours and
41 minutes of leisure.

11
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:28.860
See the pattern?

12
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:34.940
3 hours, 58, 4 hours, 3, 4 hours, 41.

13
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.440
They sit closer together
than almost anywhere else.

14
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.340
That's the most
balanced day of the 35.

15
00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.900
My 4 hours, 41 minutes of leisure is

16
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:46.840
1 hour and 19 minutes
more than Sofía gets.

17
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.660
But here's the thing about home.

18
00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:53.960
In Australia, women do 139 minutes
more unpaid work a day than men.

19
00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:58.460
That's 5 hours and 11 minutes
against 2 hours and 52 minutes.

20
00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.580
Retirement, around 65.

21
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.300
Almost exactly the
35 country average.

22
00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.760
That's my day in Australia.

23
00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:05.733
Cheers.
